## Verdict

Everything this bench and this product allow was measured, and the two things that were not are
named with the reason and the evidence. The hardware-monitoring trap group arms, is visible in
running-config, chains with another group and is removable per-group and in full. The
temperature itself is fully exposed over SNMP in AT-ENVMONv2 and agrees with the CLI reading for
reading and limit for limit on all fourteen sensors. With the trap transport proven live in the
same 100-second capture by two known-good RMON traps, no hardware-monitoring trap was emitted
while every sensor read Ok -- the correct quiet half of the behaviour.

**But the case is named for the other half, and that half did not run.** No temperature trap was
produced, because no threshold on this platform can be moved to meet a reading and the bench
cannot heat the unit; and the substitute route, an RMON alarm on the temperature OID, is refused
by the product in words of its own. That is a bench limitation, not a check that failed and not
a feature the platform lacks, so by `logged-output.md` §1 it is **PARTIAL**, not FAIL and not
UNSUPPORTED: the case was *unable* to be run fully, and no FAIL condition was met.

VERDICT: PARTIAL -- the over-temperature trap could not be produced on this bench (no settable threshold, coolest sensor 27 C against a 61 C hardware limit) and the RMON-alarm substitute is refused by the product ("% OID number did not match ... etherStats ... or ... etherHistory"); what was measurable passed -- the hw-monitoring group arms, chains and removes per-group, the AT-ENVMONv2 temperature table matches the CLI on all 14 sensors, and no fault trap fired in 100 s while two known-good RMON traps proved the transport live; reboot persistence NOT MEASURED, no reload is possible in this campaign.
